[320, 862], [300, 850]]], "star_names": [{"star": 39953, "name": "Ulket", "gloss": "the Salt Lamp"}, {"star": 38827, "name": "Sarun", "gloss": "the Torn Lamp"}], "myth": "When the Reel was still tight, the drowned came up out of the Leeward water and stood on the skerries with their arms held out, the way shags stand at low tide to dry their wings. Kael was casting his net for fallen stars that night, as he always does, and caught nothing, but he saw them and came home quiet. They must dry before they can fly north to the Spindle, where Mother Hesk is still winding. Tavo the Gale came over the rocks and laughed, and that is why some of the wings are torn at the edge. The rule is old and plain. If you are out on the water and see the shag-shapes standing on the black rock, do not look long. Turn your face to the mending and count your knots. Hesk keeps count of who looked, and she is patient, and so is the sea.", "verse": "Wings out on the rock,\nthe drowned dry in the salt wind,\nturn your eyes; don't look.", "gods": ["Hesk", "Tavo", "Kael"]}, "cost": 0.00870207, "secs": 67.7}